diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 4479b53..5a14d53 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -15,3 +15,33 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Account security and passkeys
+
+Sign-in (`/devtools-times/signin`), sign-up (`/devtools-times/signup`), and account
+security (`/devtools-times/account/settings`) share a passkey-first interface.
+Users can create password-free accounts, authenticate with a discoverable passkey,
+add and name multiple passkeys, rename or remove them, and verify their identity
+with a passkey or password before sensitive changes. The last passkey cannot be
+removed from an account without another sign-in method. Password registration
+remains available for unsupported browsers.
+
+The same-origin `api/auth/*` routes use SimpleWebAuthn for server-side verification
+and Node's built-in SQLite for accounts, public credentials, expiring challenges,
+and opaque sessions. Node 22.13+ and HTTPS (or localhost) are required. The relying
+party ID and expected origin come from the request URL, so passkeys are specific
+to the hostname where they were created. Biometric data never reaches the server.
+Sessions use HttpOnly, SameSite cookies; credential mutation requests require a
+matching Origin header. Reauthentication is valid for five minutes. Requests are
+rate limited per client address and action within each process.
+
+`AUTH_DATABASE_PATH` sets the SQLite file location (default: `.data/auth.sqlite`).
+Use a persistent private volume and backups; for multiple hosts, replace this
+single-host store and rate limiter with shared infrastructure. Configure trusted
+proxy handling so Astro receives the correct origin and client address.
+
+These accounts are local to this application. The previous forms used an external
+sample password API without an application session. Existing accounts at that
+external service are not migrated into the local account store.
+
+Validation: `pnpm run build`. No running server is needed for the build.
